{%- comment -%}
  Final Sale — reference only, not part of the Next.js build.

  Renders the custom.final_sale product metafield (written from the Lela dashboard's
  Products & Inventory → "+ Add Final Sale" flow) directly on the product page. Purely a
  Liquid read — no API calls, no JS needed, since the value already lives on the product.

  Setup:
  1. Shopify admin → Online Store → Themes → Edit code → Snippets → Add a new snippet
     → name it "final-sale" → paste this file's contents.
  2. Render it from your product template (e.g. main-product.liquid), near the
     add-to-cart button, wherever it should catch a buyer's eye before checkout:
       {% render 'final-sale', product: product %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign final_sale = product.metafields.custom.final_sale.value -%}
{%- if final_sale != blank -%}
  <div class="final-sale-note">
    <p class="final-sale-note__label">Final Sale</p>
    <p class="final-sale-note__text">{{ final_sale }}</p>
  </div>

  <style>
    .final-sale-note { margin: 1rem 0; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-left: 3px solid #8A3B2B; background: #FBF3EC; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; }
    .final-sale-note__label { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 0.9rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: #8A3B2B; }
    .final-sale-note__text { margin: 0; font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.4; }
  </style>
{%- endif -%}
